{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-594f6782-31b1-48ed-9e91-b6c6c9cad750","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f06ad5044b9e2e4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-srp7jxon/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E001.md","content":"# Console idle and stale resource reports\n\n## Description\n\nDeliver idle and stale resource reporting in the RHOAI web console: a\nper-project idle-workbench report and a stale pipeline-run report, each\nexportable as CSV. Cluster administrators get a single place to see which\nresources are sitting idle — workbenches nobody has touched in weeks that keep\ntheir volumes and reservations, and old completed pipeline runs accumulating\nstorage — so they can reclaim capacity with confidence. No new backend data\ncollection is built: the reports surface data the platform already tracks\n(notebook-controller last-activity timestamps and Kubeflow Pipelines run\ncompletion metadata).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a per-project idle-workbench report to the web console showing, for each\n  workbench: last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n  tracking), owner, and reserved resources (volumes, reservations).\n- Add a stale pipeline-run report to the web console showing completed\n  pipeline runs older than a configurable age, with their retained artifacts,\n  sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- Implement the configurable age threshold for the stale-run report (default\n  value is an implementation decision for the team).\n- Implement CSV export of either report (administrators can export the\n  idle-workbench report or the stale pipeline-run report).\n- Surface both reports in the console's existing project-scoped navigation and\n  views, consistent with how the console already lists workbenches and pipeline\n  runs.\n- Verify the passive data sources as part of this work (no code changes in\n  those components — see Acceptance Criteria).\n\nOut of scope: automated reclamation or deletion of idle resources, and\ncost/chargeback calculations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project with workbenches of varying activity, when an administrator\n  opens the idle-workbench report, then each workbench is listed with its last\n  activity, owner, and reserved resources, and the last-activity values match\n  the notebook controller's per-kernel activity tracking (validated against\n  the culler's view of the same workbenches).\n- Given a project with completed pipeline runs of varying age, when an\n  administrator opens the stale pipeline-run report with a configured age\n  threshold, then only completed runs older than the threshold are listed,\n  together with their retained artifacts, and the run completion metadata\n  matches what Kubeflow Pipelines reports through its v2 API for the same\n  project.\n- Given either report is displayed, when the administrator triggers CSV\n  export, then a CSV file is produced containing the report's rows and\n  columns.\n- Given a different age threshold is configured, when the stale pipeline-run\n  report is reloaded, then the report reflects the new threshold without a\n  console redeployment.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n  reserved resources) sourced from notebook controller activity tracking.\n- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n  run metadata.\n- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report — bundled because it is a\n  presentation mode of the same report views and shares their data structures\n  and UI surface; it is not independently schedulable from the reports\n  themselves.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30621,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a4c1ac8b89ff650","agent_id":"ad11b276ed769c788","session_id":"f3aaeace-1d3c-447c-aa51-e85705230f1b","uuid":"e2c3d50d-7547-4e32-96ca-571038f62b0b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:08:32.195Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016"}
