{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a955657f0b51a019","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n3\tepic_count: 2\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9016\n11\t\n12\tIdle resource reporting in the web console.\n13\t\n14\t## Triage\n15\t\n16\tNot below-threshold: the strategy spans three components (web console reading\n17\tfrom two architecturally distinct backend data sources — the notebook\n18\tcontroller's activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata) and includes\n19\ta substantive documentation work stream (HLR-4 authors new doc topics, not\n20\tincidental touch-ups). Not docs-only: the RHOAI web console requires code\n21\tchanges. Full decomposition follows.\n22\t\n23\t## Epic List\n24\t\n25\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n26\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Console idle and stale resource reports | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E002 | Document idle resource reports and safe reclamation | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P2 |\n29\t\n30\t## Component Analysis\n31\t\n32\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Classification | Handling |\n33\t|--------------------|---------------------|----------------|----------|\n34\t| RHOAI web console | Dashboard | Active (code changes: new report views + CSV export) | Epic RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 |\n35\t| Notebook controller | Notebooks | Passive (no code changes — last-activity data already tracked per kernel) | Validation acceptance criteria on RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 |\n36\t| Kubeflow Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | Passive (no code changes — run completion metadata already retained) | Validation acceptance criteria on RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 |\n37\t\n38\tComponent mappings (all verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`):\n39\t\"RHOAI web console\" → `Dashboard`; \"Notebook controller\" → `Notebooks`;\n40\t\"Kubeflow Pipelines\" → `Data Science Pipelines`. The passive components are\n41\tvalidated by the implementing Dashboard team (both surface data through\n42\texisting Kubernetes CRs / the KFP v2 REST API the Dashboard already reads), so\n43\tno separate validation epics are generated.\n44\t\n45\t## Dependency DAG\n46\t\n47\t```mermaid\n48\tgraph TD\n49\t    RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 --> RHAISTRAT-9016-E002\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\t## DAG Justification\n53\t\n54\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n55\t|------|------|-----------|\n56\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 → RHAISTRAT-9016-E002 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | The documentation describes the reports and reclamation steps that the implementation epic delivers; it must be written against what was actually built. |\n57\t\n58\tNo other edges: both reports (HLR-1, HLR-2) are built in the same component by\n59\tthe same team on the same console reporting surface, so they form one epic\n60\t(boundary rule 2 — same component + same team + same logical change). CSV\n61\texport (HLR-3) is a presentation mode of the same report views and shares their\n62\tdata structures and UI surface, so it is bundled rather than split. There are\n63\tno external dependencies, no new components to onboard (all three components\n64\thave architecture-context files and are Konflux-onboarded), and no open\n65\tquestions, so no Investigation epics are needed.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n68\t\n69\t| HLR | Priority | Epic | Notes |\n70\t|-----|----------|------|-------|\n71\t| HLR-1 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Per-project idle-workbench report sourced from notebook controller activity tracking |\n72\t| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Stale pipeline-run report sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata |\n73\t| HLR-3 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 (bundled) — CSV export is a presentation mode of the same report views built for HLR-1/HLR-2; it shares their data structures and UI surface, so a separate epic would build the same surface twice and is not independently schedulable | |\n74\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E002 | Documentation of reports and safe reclamation steps |\n75\t\n76\tAll four HLRs are covered; none are orphaned.\n77\t\n78\t## Health Warnings\n79\t\n80\t- **Missing strategy sections:** the strategy omits the Impacted Teams table,\n81\t  Dependencies table, formal Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and\n82\t  non-functional requirements. Teams were derived from the architecture-context\n83\t  owning teams (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard). This is a strategy-quality gap,\n84\t  not a decomposition blocker.\n85\t- **Configurable-age default unspecified:** HLR-2's \"configurable age\" default\n86\t  value is an implementation detail for the team; captured as scope, not an\n87\t  unknown requiring investigation.\n88\t- **Passive-component assumption:** the decomposition relies on the strategy's\n89\t  premise that notebook-controller last-activity tracking and KFP run\n90\t  completion metadata are sufficient data sources. Architecture context\n91\t  corroborates both (last activity tracked per kernel through Jupyter server\n92\t  API probes; KFP v2 REST API with runs surfaced in the Dashboard), and the\n93\t  premise is verified as acceptance criteria on RHAISTRAT-9016-E001.\n94\t\n95\t## Tiered Delivery\n96\t\n97\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing.\n98\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dbcee5b3faed2c5","agent_id":"a99eb069722dd97a6","session_id":"f3aaeace-1d3c-447c-aa51-e85705230f1b","uuid":"829977d8-f594-4bdc-9a89-69a2c4ae46b9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:10:17.244Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a955657f0b51a019","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
