n51\t  reclaim capacity from idle workbenches and stale pipeline runs, with\n52\t  cautions about data that is lost when resources are reclaimed.\n53\t- Content follows the Red Hat docs content process and tooling.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Documentation topics exist covering both reports, their columns and data\n58\t  sources, the configurable age threshold, and CSV export.\n59\t- A safe-reclamation procedure is documented, including cautions for actions\n60\t  that permanently remove data (volume deletion, artifact cleanup).\n61\t- All documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented reports\n62\t  and accurately reflects the shipped behavior (column names, navigation\n63\t  location, configuration mechanism).\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dbcee5b3faed2c5","agent_id":"a99eb069722dd97a6","session_id":"f3aaeace-1d3c-447c-aa51-e85705230f1b","uuid":"b16a23de-82f2-4e1d-b228-635e3686ef0a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:10:20.278Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fc4cc69c37d20c5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
